{
  "id": "fluency-l1-square-root-of-minus-one",
  "lesson": "l1-square-root-of-minus-one",
  "title": "Fluency: complex arithmetic",
  "n": 20,
  "pass": 0.9,
  "minutes": 12,
  "families": [
    {
      "id": "multiply",
      "weight": 2,
      "skill": "multiply two complex numbers",
      "vars": {
        "a": { "int": [-6, 6], "not": [0] },
        "b": { "int": [-6, 6], "not": [0] },
        "c": { "int": [-6, 6], "not": [0] },
        "d": { "int": [-6, 6], "not": [0] }
      },
      "let": {
        "ac": "a*c",
        "ad": "a*d",
        "bc": "b*c",
        "bd": "b*d",
        "re": "a*c - b*d",
        "im": "a*d + b*c"
      },
      "where": ["a*c - b*d != 0", "a*d + b*c != 0"],
      "prompt": "Work out $({a}{b:+c}i)({c}{d:+c}i)$. Give one answer $p + qi$.",
      "widget": { "kind": "expression", "answer": "{re}{im:+c}i", "form": "rectangular", "keyboard": "algebra" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "i-squared-plus-one", "tex": "{poly(i; im, ac + bd)}", "line": "You used $i^2 = +1$, so ${mono(i; bd, 2)}$ became ${bd}$. It is ${-bd}$." },
        { "id": "parts-only", "tex": "{poly(i; bd, ac)}", "line": "You multiplied real by real and $i$ part by $i$ part only. The cross terms ${mono(i; ad, 1)}$ and ${mono(i; bc, 1)}$ count too." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "The four products are ${ac}$, ${mono(i; ad, 1)}$, ${mono(i; bc, 1)}$ and ${mono(i; bd, 2)}$.",
        "With $i^2 = -1$ the last one is ${-bd}$, so the real part is ${re}$ and the $i$ part is ${im}$.",
        "So the product is ${re}{im:+c}i$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "divide",
      "weight": 2,
      "skill": "divide by a complex number",
      "vars": {
        "c": { "int": [-4, 4], "not": [0] },
        "d": { "int": [-4, 4], "not": [0] },
        "e": { "int": [-5, 5], "not": [0] },
        "f": { "int": [-5, 5], "not": [0] }
      },
      "let": {
        "nr": "c*e - d*f",
        "ni": "c*f + d*e",
        "m": "c^2 + d^2",
        "tr": "e*m",
        "ti": "f*m",
        "pr": "(c*e - d*f)/c",
        "qi": "(c*f + d*e)/d"
      },
      "where": ["c*e - d*f != 0", "c*f + d*e != 0"],
      "prompt": "Work out $\\dfrac{{{nr}{ni:+c}i}}{{{c}{d:+c}i}}$. Give one answer $p + qi$.",
      "widget": { "kind": "expression", "answer": "{e}{f:+c}i", "form": "rectangular", "keyboard": "algebra" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "part-by-part", "tex": "{pr:frac}{qi:+cfrac}i", "line": "You divided part by part: ${nr}$ by ${c}$ and ${ni}$ by ${d}$. Division does not split like that." },
        { "id": "bottom-i-squared", "tex": "{e*m/(c^2 - d^2):frac}{f*m/(c^2 - d^2):+cfrac}i", "line": "Your bottom used $i^2 = +1$. In fact $({c}{d:+c}i)({c}{-d:+c}i) = {m}$.", "when": "abs(c) != abs(d)" }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "Multiply top and bottom by the conjugate ${c}{-d:+c}i$. The bottom becomes ${c:()}^2 + {d:()}^2 = {m}$.",
        "The top becomes $({nr}{ni:+c}i)({c}{-d:+c}i) = {tr}{ti:+c}i$.",
        "Divide both parts by ${m}$: the answer is ${e}{f:+c}i$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "complex-roots",
      "weight": 2,
      "skill": "solve a quadratic with no real roots",
      "vars": {
        "p": { "int": [-5, 5], "not": [0] },
        "q": { "int": [1, 6] },
        "v": { "pick": ["x", "z"] }
      },
      "let": {
        "b": "-2*p",
        "k": "p^2 + q^2",
        "disc": "4*p^2 - 4*(p^2 + q^2)",
        "nb": "2*p",
        "q2": "2*q"
      },
      "prompt": "Solve ${poly(v; 1, b, k)} = 0$. Give both roots.",
      "widget": { "kind": "expression", "answers": ["{p}{q:+c}i", "{p}{-q:+c}i"], "unordered": true, "keyboard": "algebra" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "not-halved", "tex": "{p}{q2:+c}i, {p}{-q2:+c}i", "line": "You took $\\sqrt{{{disc}}} = {q2}i$ but did not divide it by $2$." },
        { "id": "plus-b", "tex": "{-p}{q:+c}i, {-p}{-q:+c}i", "line": "You used $+b$ on top. The formula starts with $-b = {nb}$." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "The discriminant is ${b:()}^2 - 4 \\times {k} = {disc}$, and $\\sqrt{{{disc}}} = {q2}i$.",
        "So ${v} = \\dfrac{{{nb} \\pm {q2}i}}{{2}}$, which is ${p} \\pm {q:c}i$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "power-of-i",
      "weight": 1,
      "skill": "work out a power of i",
      "vars": {
        "n": { "int": [10, 199] }
      },
      "let": {
        "r": "n % 4",
        "qt": "floor(n / 4)",
        "s": "if(n % 4 < 2, 1, -1)",
        "t": "n % 2"
      },
      "where": ["n % 4 != 0"],
      "prompt": "Work out $i^{{{n}}}$.",
      "widget": { "kind": "expression", "answer": "{mono(i; s, t)}", "form": "rectangular", "keyboard": "algebra" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "even-is-positive", "tex": "1", "line": "You saw an even power and expected a positive answer. Even powers alternate: $i^2 = -1$, $i^4 = 1$.", "when": "r == 2" },
        { "id": "odd-sign", "tex": "{mono(i; -s, 1)}", "line": "You have the wrong sign: $i^3 = i^2 \\times i = -i$.", "when": "t == 1" }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "The powers of $i$ repeat every 4: $i, -1, -i, 1$.",
        "${n} = 4 \\times {qt} + {r}$, so $i^{{{n}}} = (i^4)^{{{qt}}} \\times {mono(i; 1, r)} = {mono(i; s, t)}$."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
